    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1138">

                <pb facs="1088" n="1076" xml:id="pg1076"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2367/16: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-25T19:00:00+02:00">August 25, 1943—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1471. I have been informed today that Turkish Government has accepted validity of
                    argument that the seven survivors of the crew of the Liberator which crashed off
                    coast of southern Turkey be regarded as “shipwrecked mariners” (my 1388R, August
                    8) and has ordered their release.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d1138-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Please inform General Arnold.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Cairo for General Breton [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Brereton</hi>].<anchor n="36" xml:id="d1138-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1138-f1" n="35" xml:id="d1138-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 1596, September 21, 10 a.m., the Ambassador reported that the 15
                    aviators in question had been released by the Turkish Government
                    (811.2367/19).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1138-f2" n="36" xml:id="d1138-f2-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. Lewis H. Brereton, Commander, U.S. Army Forces in the Middle East
                    (USAFIME).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
